Outlined below are instructions for how to use this code to analyze the KOMP Sucrose & Oral Methamphetamine 2-bottle choice data.

The most recent scripts that should be used are housed within the QC figure expansion branch.

Beginning with downloading all raw data from JCMS to running analysis for sucrose and oral meth separately to generating a final 
cleaned data frame that includes Suc/OM data.

DOWNLOAD RAW DATA FROM JCMS
  1. Login to JCMS and navigate to Tom's Button Bar, then open Master Data Table (written in blue)
  2. In the top banner click "External Data", within the "export" section click the Excel option
  3. In the popup banner, specificy where you want the file downloaded to, click "OK"
  4. A second banner will pop-up with an "unable to append all the data" message, ignore and click "yes"
  5. Create a local folder on your laptop with the date of analysis (Ex. "2026-Apr-07")
  6. Create a subfolder called "data" and place the master data table file here

RUN SUC/OM ANALYSIS
SUC:
  1. There are separate scripts for running Suc and OM analysis and outputting QC figures.
  2. Begin by downloading and opening the "Sucrose_RCode_MRPathfix.Rmd" R-markdown file from Github.
  3. Scroll to line 100 and replace the file path with the correct path for where the Master data table is located on your computer 
      (should be within the folder outlined in the previous section)
      NOTE: for PC users you may need to include double "\" as shown in my wd format.
  4. Run the entire script. Analysis and QC figure generation should be complete in less than 15 minutes and will be output to a subfolder 
      within your parent analysis folder.
OM:
  5. Download and open the "OM_Code_withSexDiff.Rmd" R-markdown file from Github.
  6. Scroll to line 120 and replace the file path with the correct path for the master data table (this should be the same path used for the sucrose script)
    NOTE: for PC users you may need to include double "\" as shown in my wd format.
  7. Run the entire script.
  8. Run the entire script. Analysis and QC figure generation should be complete in less than 15 minutes and will be output to a subfolder 
      within your parent analysis folder.
  9. Once analysis is complete for both Sucrose and OM you will need to merge the separte, clean datasets into a single file. 

MERGING CLEAN DATA FROM SUC/OM ANALYSIS
  1. Open the "OM_Sucrose_Merged.Rmd" R-script.
  2. Scroll to line 49 and input the file path to your parent folder (Ex. "2026-Apr-07")
  3. Run the entire script.
  4. The merged data file will be placed in a folder called "Final_Merged" which is created by the script.
  

